sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-competency-08> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In the 1D artificial embryogeny model with evolvable competency, the correlation between genotypic and phenotypic fitness fell to zero within about 20 generations, so allowing competency to evolve disrupts selection's ability to pick the best structural genes.";
    dc:type "simulation-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Evolvable competency decouples genotypic from phenotypic fitness";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Shreesha L, Levin M, “Cellular Competency during Development Alters Evolutionary Dynamics in an Artificial Embryogeny Model”, Entropy (Basel, Switzerland) (2023), doi:10.3390/e25010131; section “3. Results › 3.4. Evolution Results in a High, Constant Level of Competency”. Scope: In silico 1D artificial embryos with an evolvable competency gene"
}
